            {
              "text": "Selling a **$10M+ residential property** places you in the absolute top tier of the South Australian property market. In Adelaide, eight-figure sales are historic events, typically concentrated in prestigious pockets like **Medindie, Unley Park, Gilberton, North Adelaide, Walkerville, Springfield**, and select beachfront addresses along **Glenelg**. \n\nBecause the buyer pool at this price point is very small, success depends less on generic open inspections and more on **private networks, discretion, and interstate/international reach**. \n\nThe following agencies and specialist agents have the strongest, proven track records for ultra-prestige and record-breaking sales in Adelaide:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Ultra-Prestige Record Holders\n\n#### **Booth Real Estate — Jamie Brown**\n* **Track Record:** Jamie Brown is arguably Adelaide’s most prolific agent when it comes to setting state residential price records. \n* **Key Credentials:** He has brokered several of South Australia's most historic trophy transactions, including **3 Victoria Avenue, Unley Park** (sold for $11.2M), **11 The Avenue, Medindie**, and the grand historic estate **Ivanhoe** in Gilberton.\n* **Best For:** Unmatched off-market negotiation and a private \"black book\" connecting local old-wealth families, interstate corporate executives, and international high-net-worth individuals.\n\n#### **Williams Luxury Real Estate — John Williams & Stephanie Williams**\n* **Track Record:** A boutique agency dedicated almost exclusively to Adelaide’s top-end luxury market. \n* **Key Credentials:** Williams handled the groundbreaking sale of ***Elysian* (9 Robe Terrace, Medindie)**, one of the earliest public eight-figure transactions in South Australia. They routinely dominate the $4M–$10M+ bracket across Adelaide’s eastern suburbs and coastal belts.\n* **Best For:** World-class digital and visual presentation, high-impact national editorial placement, and high visibility among active luxury upgraders.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major Prestige Powerhouses & Boutiques\n\n#### **TOOP+TOOP — Sally Cameron / Bronte Manuel**\n* **Track Record:** One of South Australia’s longest-standing and most decorated prestige agencies. \n* **Key Credentials:** Individual lead agents like **Sally Cameron** have repeatedly achieved the highest residential sales prices in the state across various years and hold numerous street and suburb records in the eastern suburbs and North Adelaide. \n* **Best For:** Proprietary buyer database technology (*ToopVault*) and corporate relocation reach.\n\n#### **Alexander Real Estate — Penny Riggs**\n* **Track Record:** Known for handling elite character and estate homes across Adelaide's inner-south and eastern suburbs.\n* **Key Credentials:** Notably handled the landmark on-market sale of **4 Victoria Avenue, Unley Park**, which surpassed $10.5M.\n* **Best For:** High-touch, discreet representation of sprawling heritage estates and architectural mansions.\n\n#### **Giordano & Partners — Grant Giordano**\n* **Track Record:** Founded by Grant Giordano (formerly head of South Australia Sotheby’s International Realty). \n* **Key Credentials:** Has represented trophy multi-million dollar architectural homes, coastal estates, and luxury lifestyle properties.\n* **Best For:** Direct cross-border appeal, targeting expats, interstate buyers relocating from Sydney/Melbourne, and international buyers.\n\n#### **Harris Real Estate (Harris Prestige)**\n* **Track Record:** While Harris operates across all tiers, its dedicated **Prestige division** (led by agents like Phil Harris and Arabella Hooper) commands significant high-end market share, particularly for major acreage estates, the Adelaide Hills, and premium eastern suburb homes.\n* **Best For:** Broad marketing horsepower, large agent networks, and extensive cross-selling capacity.\n\n---\n\n### How to Select the Right Agency for a $10M Listing\n\nWhen interviewing agents for a property of this caliber, ask these key questions:\n\n1. **Off-Market vs. On-Market Strategy:** At $10M+, many vendors choose to start with a confidential 30-to-60-day off-market campaign. Ask how many qualified buyers they can introduce immediately without public advertising.\n2. **Buyer Vetting Protocol:** At this price point, you must avoid \"curiosity seekers.\" Ensure the agency requires non-disclosure agreements (NDAs) and proof of funds or financial pre-qualification before booking private walkthroughs.\n3. **Interstate & International Reach:** A notable percentage of eight-figure Adelaide buyers are ex-pats returning from overseas or interstate business figures drawn to Adelaide's lifestyle and value. Ask specifically how they plan to market beyond South Australia.\n\n**Recommendation:** Invite **Jamie Brown (Booth Real Estate)**, **Stephanie & John Williams (Williams Luxury)**, and **Sally Cameron (TOOP+TOOP)** to pitch. This gives you a direct comparison between the two undisputed individual champions of Adelaide's $10M+ sales record alongside the state’s largest prestige corporate agency.",
